      "Turn-flow example: 1. **Ante**: Each player pays one chip to the central pot before the deal.\n2. **Turn Structure**: Players take turns clockwise, starting with the player to dealer's left.\n3. **Drawing**: On your turn, draw one card either from the top of the stock pile (face down) or take the top card of the face-up discard pile.\n4. **Knocking (Optional)**: If you believe you have the best poker hand, you may knock by knocking on the table or saying 'I knock'. This signals that play will end after each other player has one more turn.\n5. **Discarding**: After drawing (and optionally knocking), discard one card face up on the discard pile. You cannot discard the same card you just took from the discard pile in the same turn.\n6. **Immediate Knock**: A player satisfied with their original dealt hand may knock on their first turn without drawing or discarding.",
      'Scoring example: Best poker hand wins the pot. Knocker wins: others pay 2 chips each. Knocker loses: pays 2 chips to each staying player. Folders pay 1 chip to knocker. Have the highest-ranking five-card poker hand at showdown.',
